  // The store's calendar (UTC days). "when": a weekday, a weekday of the month ("firstFriday", "thirdSaturday",
  // "lastSunday"…) or a date; "months" limits it to those months, "days" makes it run several days from then. Big events:
  // "playersMax" (attendance drawn between "players" and it), "rounds": 0 (Swiss rounds by attendance), "cutAfter" and
  // "cutPoints" (a cut by record), "topCut" (a single-elimination playoff), "invitational" (only players a prize with
  // "qualifies": its id invited; "minPlayers" on a prize: only with that attendance), "tournamentMat" (played at the big
  // tournaments' table on one mat for both players, with the event's name on its crest), "roundMinutes" (the Swiss
  // rounds' time limit: then no new game begins and a game in progress gets five more turns; the playoff is untimed).
  // Kinds: draft,
  // constructed (a career deck) and commander (a career Commander deck; pods of "players" play "rounds" games against
  // computer players bringing the "decks" listed; prizes by games won). Prizes: the first
  // one that fits the player's result ("wins": at least that many match wins; "place": that place or better; neither:
  // anyone). Draft events take the week's featured set unless "set" names one; the drafted cards are the player's.
  // Constructed events take a "format": a format id from formats/ ("standard", "modern"…), the decks must be legal in it;
  // empty or absent: any cards (casual). Commander events always use the Commander format.
  "events": [
    {
      // Every day: a cheap draft against the computer; the store provides the boosters and the drafted cards are the player's.
      "id": "daily-draft", "name": "Daily draft", "when": "daily", "kind": "draft", "set": "featured",
      "players": 8, "rounds": 3, "bestOf": 1, "entry": 100,
      "prizes": [
        { "wins": 2, "boosters": 1, "reputation": 2 }
      ]
    },
    {
